<title>USA: CME March volume rises 4.7 pct year-on-year.</title>
<headline>CME March volume rises 4.7 pct year-on-year.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange (CME) said volume in March totaled 20,592,505 contracts, up 4.7 percent from the year-ago monthly level of 19,662,594 contracts.</p>
<p>Open interest at month's end stood at 6,140,579, up 11.0 percent from 5,530,699 at the end of March last year.</p>
<p>Through March, 1997's year-to-date volume totaled 53,590,562, down 0.7 percent from 53,981,092 contracts traded during the same period in 1996.</p>
<p>Major categories and volumes were as follows:</p>
<p>Futures (individual)   Mar 1997	% change	   Mar 1996</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	  10,117,388	  - 6.0	  10,763,786</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	   744,834	  +28.4	     579,885</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	   564,776	  +19.4	     473,129</p>
<p>  Swiss franc	    436,807	  +37.3	     318,047</p>
<p>  British pound	  289,352	  -17.6	     350,973</p>
<p>  Canadian dollar	295,170	  +58.2	     186,540</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		2,081,253	   +3.8	   2,005,441</p>
<p>  Live cattle	    312,120	   -6.3	     333,257</p>
<p>  Live/lean hogs	 200,276	  +33.3	     150,193</p>
<p>Options on futures</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	   2,528,838	  +20.2	   2,103,757</p>
<p>  Eurodollar midcurv   791,554	 +151.4	     314,874</p>
<p>  Swiss franc	     85,093	  +26.2		67,407</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	   169,928	  -18.2	     207,793</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	   174,343	   -8.0	     189,476</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		  517,482	   -9.1	     569,447</p>
<p>  Live cattle	     38,835	  -17.1		46,868</p>
<p>Since January 1994 CME has counted in volume anything that creates or liquidates open positions including expired options and SIMEX mutual offset transactions cleared on the CME.</p>
<p>Excluding these transactions, CME &quot;pit traded&quot; volume for March 1997 totaled 17,676,976 and year-to-day volume totaled 48,196,719.</p>
<p>-- Chicago Derivatives Desk (312) 408-8750</p>
